{% comment %}
  "Every tweak, documented" reference page.

  Built because 525 documented changes is the biggest number anyone in this
  category publishes and it was invisible: the site said "525 tweaks" on five
  pages and never once said what they were. It answers the objection that sinks
  this category ("what is it actually doing to my PC") and it targets the real
  queries: what does miztweakz change, are pc tweaks safe, 525 tweaks.

  Every figure below is counted from the app's own catalogue, src/tweaks.js, on
  2026-09-12: 525 entries across 13 categories, tiers free 10 / basic 253 /
  ultimate 262, kinds reg 234 / service 119 / appx 70 / task 60 / cmd 32, and
  the app's own risk labels, safe 414 / caution 111. If the catalogue changes,
  recount it. Do not round these or guess.
{% endcomment %}

