<section class="section animate" aria-labelledby="what-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header section-header--left">
      <span class="title-tag bar-eyebrow" aria-hidden="true">What it changes</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="what-title">Windows settings only, never your games</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-layout legal-layout--single">
      <div class="legal-prose">
        <p>
          Every one of the 525 tweaks is one of five kinds of change. There is no sixth kind,
          and none of them touch a game install.
        </p>

        <div class="glass-info-card-grid" style="margin:1.5rem 0">
          <div class="glass-info-card glass-card"><span class="info-accent"></span>
            <h3>234 registry values</h3>
            <p>Windows settings that have no switch in the Settings app: frame pacing, GPU scheduling, mouse acceleration, TCP behaviour, menu delays.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="glass-info-card glass-card"><span class="info-accent"></span>
            <h3>119 Windows services</h3>
            <p>Background services set to disabled or manual. Fax, Remote Registry, Superfetch, Windows Search and similar, none of which a gaming PC needs running.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="glass-info-card glass-card"><span class="info-accent"></span>
            <h3>70 Store app removals</h3>
            <p>Pre-installed apps you never opened. Removed with Windows' own uninstall, and every one can be reinstalled from the Microsoft Store.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="glass-info-card glass-card"><span class="info-accent"></span>
            <h3>60 scheduled tasks</h3>
            <p>Background jobs Windows runs on a timer, mostly telemetry, diagnostics and update checks that wake your machine mid-game.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="glass-info-card glass-card"><span class="info-accent"></span>
            <h3>32 commands</h3>
            <p>Power plan changes and network stack resets, the same commands you would type yourself with powercfg and netsh.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="glass-info-card glass-card" style="--color:#22c55e"><span class="info-accent"></span>
            <h3>0 changes to game files</h3>
            <p>Nothing is written into a game folder, no file is patched and nothing is injected into a running process. The app reads Fortnite's install path for one thing only: its icon.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

